Subject: allow empty tbl cells to own vertical spans
Upstream-Status: Candidate (not submitted)

A continued cell can close before appending any text. Its NULL payload
means there was no input row, but the cell is still a valid span owner.
Only compare the continuation token when an actual string exists.

--- a/tbl_data.c
+++ b/tbl_data.c
@@ -123,7 +123,8 @@
 			if (pdat == NULL)
 				break;
 			if (pdat->layout->pos != TBL_CELL_DOWN &&
-			    strcmp(pdat->string, "\\^") != 0) {
+			    (pdat->string == NULL ||
+			     strcmp(pdat->string, "\\^") != 0)) {
 				pdat->vspans++;
 				break;
 			}
